9	//! reference carries a heading with THAT number and THAT exact title, and
10	//! that the entry's word is written somewhere inside that section's text. The
11	//! second half is what makes the citation load-bearing rather than
12	//! decorative — a word could otherwise be filed under a section that never
13	//! mentions it, and the reader following the pointer would find nothing.
